 "note": "RPCS3 Core 916 (Core 915 was the 4-way comparison witness of Core 914 and is the base of nothing): Core 914 plus the corrections drawn from the build 718 journals. REWINDBOX_SPURS_RELAXED_STORE_916: with Accurate SPU Reservations off, the PUTLLC of an SPU on a SPURS header line no longer copies its whole 128-byte line over memory; the line is compared with the GETLLAR copy and each changed 16-byte lane is exchanged atomically, a plain guest store made since GETLLAR fails the PUTLLC and is never overwritten, and a PUTLLC a guest store interrupts gives back the lanes it had stored (Assassin's Creed, build 718: the lost wake-up of the SPURS kernels behind the 6 s wait of the stop sequence). REWINDBOX_GOW3_MLAA_100_916: the God of War III MLAA bypass (the existing title setting) knows the 01.00 executable, behind a content guard, at a fresh boot. Collection repairs: the stall dump lists the waiters of a lightweight condition from its own queue and the return addresses of waiting PPU threads; CONFIG_LAYERS exports the 21 lever digits (18 before: no capture could be requested); stopped report windows are compact; the report asks once per boot for the bounded PPU region profile when a PPU thread saturates a core. No resolution, precision, frame limit, SPU count or priority, GETLLAR/PUTLLC delay or LLVM option changes. SPUThread.cpp, an SPU identity input, changes in the host body of do_putllc() only (plus one include): one more exact alias in JITCacheCompatibility.cmake (Core 627 procedure, audited), identities unchanged. Host bridge 8977315e unchanged; MoltenVK dependency of run 42733987255 (library d19d3a42). Built by the RPCS3 Core route (run 42764728604, attempt 1, source 850341af; Apple host harnesses run 42764728604 on 850341af; request 1, run 42763953223, had been refused by the source closure before any compile). Verified offline on the downloaded artifacts with the repository verifier (pin_errors and bundle). Not measured on the iPhone; no FPS claim.",
